    "description": "Creates or replaces ONE ISO week. This is a full replacement within that week: any existing day, meal, step, shopping list, category, item or prep session that is not in the submitted document is deleted. To change one thing, call get_week, edit the document, and submit all of it. Other weeks are never touched. Use client-generated lowercase UUIDs for new records and keep existing ids to preserve them. Optional values must be explicit nulls; array order is stored order. Every prep session needs a weekday, 1-7 (Monday=1) or null; a null weekday shows the session on no day. To create a week that has no saved plan yet, omit expectedRevision; if a plan is already saved, this returns revision_conflict. To replace a saved week, pass the revision from get_week as expectedRevision; a mismatch returns revision_conflict, after which you must fetch the week again and reconcile. There is no force option. The whole save is one transaction: an invalid document changes nothing. Returns the committed week and its new revision.",
